From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:59:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: waiting requests whose client left are
 dropped at once, TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0073)

With --parallel, a request waiting while every lane was busy kept waiting after its client left, until a lane freed,
and a reply whose connection failed mid-stream decoded on. MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.6 drops such requests at once, in
queue order, with patch 0073-glm-queued-cancellation: each waiting caller polls its client about every 0.1 s, a
disconnect latches, and only the scheduler removes the request (so rank 1 never sees it); a stream already admitted
ends after its round and its caller raises RequestCancelled once the decoder let it go; a delivery failure stops the
stream the same way and is raised after the decoder's cleanup. On the AFD split the scheduler is the attention node's
(rank 0 of world 1). This ports it behind a switch of this tree's own, off by default:

- multi.py: GlmScheduler.queued_cancel (TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL, read with recipe_switch); _submit_polled (the patch's
  submit body), _cancel_item and _cancel_waiting, verbatim; their calls in _admit and _iteration as in the patch, and
  in this tree's _admit_sjf (TF_GLM_PREFILL_ORDER=sjf). Changes for this tree: _submit_polled stamps the arrival under
  sjf as submit does; _cancel_waiting keeps TensorFold v0.6.5's close() stop entry (a None item) in the queue; _admit
  skips the check for a None item.
- engine.py: a startup line when the switch is on.
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "GLM queued cancellation".

Unset, submit, _admit, _admit_sjf and _iteration take the same paths as before.

Tests: tests/test_glm_queued_cancel.py (3, CPU, no Torch): the recipe's tools/test_queued_cancellation.py checks (by
desy0305), their bodies verbatim, on this tree's GlmScheduler loaded from the source as the recipe's tool loads it:
all 21 pass with the switch on (the recipe's tree at 68ebd67 passes the same 21 with the tool itself); with the switch
off, the tool's --expect-stock check reproduces the wait before 0073; the switch's values.

Credit: patch 0073 was written by desy0305 (https://github.com/desy0305) in
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold pull request #51, with the delivery-failure handling from
johnwhited's (https://github.com/johnwhited) pull request #48; MiaAI-Lab applied it as contributed in recipe commit
5859365 (v1.6), Apache License 2.0, with tools/test_queued_cancellation.py.

