+## GLM queued cancellation (TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL)
+
+The `TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL=1` paths of `families/glm5_next/cuda/multi.py`'s `GlmScheduler` (`_submit_polled`,
+`_cancel_item`, `_cancel_waiting`, and their calls in `submit`, `_admit`, `_admit_sjf` and `_iteration`: a request
+waiting while every lane is busy, whose client left, is dropped at once instead of when a lane frees, and a reply whose
+delivery fails ends after its round) are MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/68ebd67)
+patch 0073-glm-queued-cancellation (v1.6, recipe commit
+[`5859365`](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/commit/585936585de470a0b687a998f48b636bd22e440d)),
+written by [desy0305](https://github.com/desy0305) in
+[pull request #51](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/pull/51) and applied by
+MiaAI-Lab as contributed; its delivery-failure handling comes from [johnwhited](https://github.com/johnwhited)'s
+[pull request #48](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/pull/48). The checks in
+`tests/test_glm_queued_cancel.py` are the recipe's `tools/test_queued_cancellation.py` (by desy0305), verbatim but for
+how they are run. Both are under the recipe's Apache License 2.0 (see [the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)).
+Changes in the port: the recipe always runs it, and here it is off unless `TF_GLM_QUEUED_CANCEL=1`
+(`GlmScheduler.queued_cancel`); unset, `submit`, `_admit` and `_iteration` run as before. The patch's `submit` body is
+`_submit_polled`, which also stamps a request's arrival under `TF_GLM_PREFILL_ORDER=sjf`; the dropping also runs in
+this tree's shortest-first admission (`_admit_sjf`), and `_cancel_waiting` leaves TensorFold v0.6.5's `close()` stop
+entry in the queue.
